msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR pojasevi (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) bilježi "
"radijancije na vrhu atmosfere u šest kanala reflektiranog sunčevog zračenja "
"razlučivosti 500 m: S1 (0,555 µm, vegetacija/aerosol), S2 (0,659 µm, "
"NDVI/aerosol), S3 (0,865 µm, NDVI/označavanje oblaka), S4 (1,375 µm, "
"otkrivanje cirusa), S5 (1,61 µm, led/snijeg/vegetacija) i S6 (2,25 µm, "
"stanje vegetacije). Svaki pojas dostupan je u nadirnom i kosom pogledu, što "
"omogućuje opažanje kopnenih i oceanskih površina pod dvama kutovima. "
"Proizvod L1B sadrži georeferencirane, kalibrirane radijancije dobivene "
"kalibracijom signala, ponovnim uzorkovanjem na mrežu i označavanjem oblaka.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR termalni infracrveni pojasevi (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) bilježi "
"svjetlinske temperature na vrhu atmosfere u tri termalna infracrvena kanala "
"razlučivosti 1 km: S7 (3,74 µm, temperatura površine mora/kopna i "
"otkrivanje požara), S8 (10,85 µm, temperatura površine mora/kopna i "
"otkrivanje požara) i S9 (12,0 µm, temperatura površine mora/kopna). Svaki "
"pojas dostupan je u nadirnom i kosom pogledu, što omogućuje opažanje pod "
"dvama kutovima radi bolje atmosferske korekcije i dobivanja temperature "
"površine. Proizvod L1B sadrži georeferencirane, kalibrirane svjetlinske "
"temperature dobivene kalibracijom signala, ponovnim uzorkovanjem na mrežu i "
"označavanjem oblaka.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Termalni IR pojasevi emisije požara\n"
"\n"
"Instrument Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) "
"ima dva namjenska kanala (F1 i F2) namijenjena otkrivanju temperature "
"površine zemljišta (LST). Kanal F2, sa središnjom valnom duljinom od 10854 "
"nm, mjeri u termalnom infracrvenom području (TIR). Vrlo je koristan za "
"praćenje požara i događaja visokih temperatura razlučivosti 1 km.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Visina baze oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Visina baze oblaka izmjerena u metrima (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Tlak na bazi oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Tlak izmjeren na bazi oblaka u paskalima (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Effective radiometric cloud fraction\n"
"\n"
"Effective radiometric cloud fraction represents the portion of the Earth's "
"surface covered by clouds, divided by the total surface. Clouds have "
"shielding, albedo, and in-cloud absorption effects on trace gas retrieval. "
"The effective radiometric cloud fraction is an important parameter to "
"correct these effects."
msgstr ""
"# Efektivni radiometrijski udio oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Efektivni radiometrijski udio oblaka predstavlja dio Zemljine površine "
"prekriven oblacima, podijeljen s ukupnom površinom. Oblaci imaju učinke "
"zasjenjenja, albeda i apsorpcije unutar oblaka na određivanje plinova u "
"tragovima. Efektivni radiometrijski udio oblaka važan je parametar za "
"ispravljanje tih učinaka."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Optička debljina oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Debljina oblaka ključan je parametar za karakterizaciju optičkih svojstava "
"oblaka. To je mjera količine sunčeve svjetlosti koja prolazi kroz oblak do "
"Zemljine površine. Što je veća optička debljina oblaka, to oblak više "
"raspršuje i reflektira sunčevu svjetlost. Tamnoplava pokazuje gdje su "
"vrijednosti optičke debljine oblaka niske, a crvena veću optičku debljinu "
"oblaka."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Visina vrha oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Visina vrha oblaka izmjerena u metrima (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Tlak na vrhu oblaka\n"
"\n"
"Tlak izmjeren na vrhu oblaka u paskalima (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Termalni pojas 10\n"
"\n"
"Ova termalna vizualizacija temelji se na pojasu 10 (pojas je područje "
"elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u "
"različitim pojasevima). Na središnjoj valnoj duljini od 10895 nm mjeri u "
"termalnom infracrvenom području (TIR). Umjesto mjerenja temperature zraka, "
"kao što to rade meteorološke postaje, pojas 10 bilježi temperaturu samog "
"tla, koje je često puno toplije. Termalni pojas 10 koristan je za dobivanje "
"temperatura površine i prikuplja se razlučivosti od 100 metara.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1).\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vegetacije (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vegetacije jednostavan je, ali "
"učinkovit indeks za kvantificiranje zelene vegetacije. To je mjera zdravlja "
"vegetacije na temelju toga kako biljke reflektiraju svjetlost na određenim "
"valnim duljinama. Raspon vrijednosti NDVI-ja je od -1 do 1. Negativne "
"vrijednosti NDVI-ja (vrijednosti koje se približavaju -1) odgovaraju vodi. "
"Vrijednosti blizu nule (-0,1 do 0,1) uglavnom odgovaraju neplodnim "
"područjima stijena, pijeska ili snijega. Niske, pozitivne vrijednosti "
"predstavljaju grmlje i travnjake (otprilike 0,2 do 0,4), dok visoke "
"vrijednosti ukazuju na umjerene i tropske kišne šume (vrijednosti koje se "
"približavaju 1).\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index as "
"it corrects for soil background signals and atmospheric influences. It is "
"very useful in areas of dense canopy cover. The range of values for EVI is "
"-1 to 1, with healthy vegetation generally around 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More infos [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) "
"and [here.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"
msgstr ""
"# Poboljšani indeks vegetacije (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"Poboljšani indeks vegetacije (EVI) je „optimiziran” indeks vegetacije jer "
"ispravlja signale tla u pozadini i atmosferske utjecaje. Vrlo je koristan u "
"područjima guste krošnje. Raspon vrijednosti EVI-ja je od -1 do 1, a zdrava "
"vegetacija uglavnom je oko 0,20 do 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) i "
"[ovdje.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosferski otporan indeks vegetacije (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Atmosferski otporan indeks vegetacije (ARVI) je indeks vegetacije koji "
"minimizira učinke atmosferskog raspršenja. Najkorisniji je za regije s "
"visokim sadržajem atmosferskih aerosola (magla, prašina, dim, onečišćenje "
"zraka). Raspon ARVI-ja je od -1 do 1, a zelena vegetacija uglavnom se "
"nalazi između vrijednosti 0,20 i 0,80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) i "
"[ovdje.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-"
"your-vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Indeks vegetacije prilagođen tlu (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Indeks vegetacije prilagođen tlu sličan je normaliziranom diferencijalnom "
"indeksu vegetacije (NDVI), ali se koristi u područjima s niskim "
"vegetacijskim pokrovom (< 40 %). Indeks je transformacijska tehnika koja "
"smanjuje utjecaj svjetline tla na spektralne indekse vegetacije koji "
"uključuju crvene i bliske infracrvene (NIR) valne duljine. Indeks je "
"koristan pri analizi mladih usjeva, sušnih regija s rijetkom vegetacijom i "
"izloženih površina tla.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) i "
"[ovdje.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-"
"your-vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Modificirani indeks refleksije antocijana (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Antocijani su pigmenti uobičajeni u višim biljkama koji uzrokuju njihovu "
"crvenu, plavu i ljubičastu boju. Pružaju vrijedne informacije o fiziološkom "
"stanju biljaka jer se smatraju pokazateljima različitih vrsta biljnog "
"stresa. Refleksija antocijana najveća je oko 550 nm. Međutim, iste valne "
"duljine reflektira i klorofil. Kako bi se antocijani izolirali, oduzima se "
"spektralni pojas od 700 nm, koji reflektira samo klorofil, a ne antocijane.\n"
"\n"
"Za ispravak gustoće i debljine lista osnovnom se ARI indeksu dodaje bliski "
"infracrveni spektralni pojas (na preporučenim valnim duljinama od 760-800 "
"nm), koji je povezan s raspršenjem na listu. Novi indeks naziva se "
"modificirani ARI ili mARI (također ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"Vrijednosti mARI-ja za ispitivana stabla u [ovom izvornom "
"članku](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) kretale "
"su se od 0 do 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Skripta Zeleni grad\n"
"\n"
"Skripta Zeleni grad namijenjena je podizanju svijesti o zelenim površinama "
"u gradovima diljem svijeta. Skripta uzima u obzir normalizirani "
"diferencijalni indeks vegetacije (NDVI) i valne duljine prave boje; "
"razdvaja izgrađena područja od onih s vegetacijom, zbog čega je korisna za "
"otkrivanje urbanih područja. Izgrađena područja prikazana su sivo, a "
"vegetacija zeleno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Skripta Urbana klasifikacija\n"
"\n"
"Skripta Urbana klasifikacija namijenjena je otkrivanju izgrađenih područja "
"razdvajanjem od neplodnog tla, vegetacije i vode. Područja s visokim "
"sadržajem vlage prikazana su plavo; područja koja upućuju na izgrađenost "
"prikazana su bijelo; područja s vegetacijom prikazana su zeleno; sve ostalo "
"upućuje na neplodno tlo i prikazano je smeđim tonovima.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_"
"classified/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Skripta Urbano zemljište u infracrvenim bojama\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta, koju je izradio Leo Tolari, kombinira vizualizaciju u pravoj "
"boji s bliskim infracrvenim (NIR) i kratkovalnim infracrvenim (SWIR) valnim "
"duljinama. Skripta bolje ističe urbana područja nego prava boja, a pritom i "
"dalje izgleda prirodno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# NDMI za stres od vlage\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vlage (NDMI) za stres od vlage može se "
"koristiti za otkrivanje navodnjavanja. Za sve vrijednosti indeksa iznad 0, "
"poznavanjem načina korištenja i pokrova zemljišta, moguće je odrediti je li "
"došlo do navodnjavanja. Poznavanjem vrste uzgajanog usjeva (npr. agrumi) "
"moguće je utvrditi je li navodnjavanje učinkovito tijekom ključne ljetne "
"sezone rasta, kao i otkriti jesu li pojedini dijelovi farme premalo ili "
"previše navodnjavani.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vlage (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vlage (NDMI) koristi se za određivanje "
"sadržaja vode u vegetaciji i praćenje suša. Raspon vrijednosti NDMI-ja je "
"od -1 do 1. Negativne vrijednosti NDMI-ja (vrijednosti koje se približavaju "
"-1) odgovaraju neplodnom tlu. Vrijednosti oko nule (-0,2 do 0,4) uglavnom "
"odgovaraju vodnom stresu. Visoke, pozitivne vrijednosti predstavljaju gustu "
"krošnju bez vodnog stresa (otprilike 0,4 do 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vode (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks vode najprikladniji je za kartiranje "
"vodenih tijela. Vrijednosti vodenih tijela veće su od 0,5. Vegetacija ima "
"manje vrijednosti. Izgrađene strukture imaju pozitivne vrijednosti između "
"nule i 0,2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) and [here.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit lažnih boja\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit lažnih boja koristi barem jednu nevidljivu valnu duljinu za "
"snimanje Zemlje. Kompozit lažnih boja koji koristi bliski infracrveni, "
"crveni i zeleni pojas vrlo je popularan (pojas je područje "
"elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u "
"različitim pojasevima). Kompozit lažnih boja najčešće se koristi za "
"procjenu gustoće i zdravlja biljaka jer biljke reflektiraju bliski "
"infracrveni i zeleni dio svjetlosti, a apsorbiraju crveni. Gradovi i "
"otkriveno tlo su sivi ili žućkastosmeđi, a voda izgleda plavo ili crno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) i [ovdje.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit lažnih boja\n"
"\n"
"Kompozit lažnih boja koristi barem jednu nevidljivu valnu duljinu za "
"snimanje Zemlje. Kompozit lažnih boja koji koristi bliski infracrveni, "
"crveni i zeleni pojas vrlo je popularan (pojas je područje "
"elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u "
"različitim pojasevima). Kompozit lažnih boja najčešće se koristi za "
"procjenu gustoće i zdravlja biljaka jer biljke reflektiraju bliski "
"infracrveni i zeleni dio svjetlosti, a apsorbiraju crveni. Gradovi i "
"otkriveno tlo su sivi ili žućkastosmeđi, a voda izgleda plavo ili crno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/)."

msgid ""
"# True color optimized\n"
"\n"
"This optimized True color script uses the visible light bands red, green "
"and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting "
"in a product with natural colours that represents the Earth as humans would "
"naturally see it. The visualisation uses highlight compression and improves "
"the contrast and color vividness through minor contrast and saturation "
"enhancement.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info for "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) "
"and for "
"[L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."
msgstr ""
"# Optimizirana prava boja\n"
"\n"
"Ova optimizirana skripta prave boje koristi pojaseve vidljive svjetlosti "
"crvene, zelene i plave u odgovarajućim kanalima crvene, zelene i plave "
"boje, što daje proizvod prirodnih boja koji prikazuje Zemlju onako kako bi "
"je ljudi prirodno vidjeli. Vizualizacija koristi kompresiju svijetlih "
"dijelova te poboljšava kontrast i živost boja blagim pojačanjem kontrasta i "
"zasićenosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija za "
"[L1C](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l1c_optimized/) i "
"za [L2A](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/l2a_optimized/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum. Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. Landsat 8-9 has 11 bands. True color composite uses visible light "
"bands red, green and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color "
"channels, resulting in a natural colored product, that is a good "
"representation of the Earth as humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit prave boje\n"
"\n"
"Senzori koje nose sateliti mogu snimati Zemlju u različitim područjima "
"elektromagnetskog spektra. Svako područje spektra naziva se pojasom. "
"Landsat 8-9 ima 11 pojaseva. Kompozit prave boje koristi pojaseve vidljive "
"svjetlosti crvene, zelene i plave u odgovarajućim kanalima crvene, zelene i "
"plave boje, što daje proizvod prirodnih boja koji dobro prikazuje Zemlju "
"onako kako bi je ljudi prirodno vidjeli.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum . Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. True color composite uses visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit prave boje\n"
"\n"
"Senzori koje nose sateliti mogu snimati Zemlju u različitim područjima "
"elektromagnetskog spektra . Svako područje spektra naziva se pojasom. "
"Kompozit prave boje koristi pojaseve vidljive svjetlosti crvene, zelene i "
"plave u odgovarajućim kanalima crvene, zelene i plave boje, što daje "
"proizvod prirodnih boja koji dobro prikazuje Zemlju onako kako bi je ljudi "
"prirodno vidjeli.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"

msgid ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"The colours of natural waters differ markedly across the globe, depending "
"on water composition and illumination conditions. Ocean colour instruments "
"measure water-leaving radiance in narrow spectral bands to retrieve "
"water-quality indicators. The true colour of natural waters is derived by "
"calculating tristimulus values — the three primaries (X, Y, Z) that specify "
"a colour stimulus as perceived by the human eye.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."
msgstr ""
"# Tristimulus\n"
"\n"
"Boje prirodnih voda znatno se razlikuju diljem svijeta, ovisno o sastavu "
"vode i uvjetima osvjetljenja. Instrumenti za boju oceana mjere radijanciju "
"koja izlazi iz vode u uskim spektralnim pojasevima kako bi dobili "
"pokazatelje kvalitete vode. Prava boja prirodnih voda dobiva se izračunom "
"tristimulusnih vrijednosti — triju primarnih vrijednosti (X, Y, Z) koje "
"određuju podražaj boje kakvim ga percipira ljudsko oko.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/tristimulus/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B05 (510 nm, cyan-green), and B02 (412.5 nm, violet) into "
"the red, green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a "
"near-infrared band used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it "
"in the red channel makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red "
"while water remains dark. B05 is sensitive to chlorophyll, sediment, "
"turbidity, and red tide, and B02 captures yellow dissolved organic matter "
"(CDOM) and detrital pigments. The composite is useful for ocean colour "
"analysis, coastal water quality monitoring, and distinguishing turbid or "
"sediment-laden waters from clear ocean.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B05, B02)\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit lažnih boja preslikava pojaseve Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 nm, "
"bliski infracrveni), B05 (510 nm, cijan-zelena) i B02 (412,5 nm, "
"ljubičasta) u crveni, zeleni i plavi kanal prikaza. B17 je bliski "
"infracrveni pojas koji se koristi za korekciju aerosola i atmosfere; "
"njegovim postavljanjem u crveni kanal vegetacija i kopnene površine "
"izgledaju jarko crveno, dok voda ostaje tamna. B05 je osjetljiv na "
"klorofil, sediment, zamućenost i crvenu plimu, a B02 bilježi žutu otopljenu "
"organsku tvar (CDOM) i detritne pigmente. Kompozit je koristan za analizu "
"boje oceana, praćenje kvalitete obalnih voda i razlikovanje mutnih ili "
"sedimentom opterećenih voda od čistog oceana.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"This false color composite maps Sentinel-3 OLCI bands B17 (865 nm, "
"near-infrared), B06 (560 nm, green), and B03 (442.5 nm, blue) into the red, "
"green, and blue display channels respectively. B17 is a near-infrared band "
"used for aerosol and atmospheric correction; placing it in the red channel "
"makes vegetation and land surfaces appear bright red while water remains "
"dark. B06 is the chlorophyll absorption minimum reference band, and B03 "
"captures chlorophyll absorption and biogeochemical properties. Compared to "
"the B17/B05/B02 composite, the shifted green and blue channels offer a "
"different sensitivity to phytoplankton and dissolved organic matter in "
"coastal and open ocean waters.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."
msgstr ""
"# RGB (B17, B06, B03)\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit lažnih boja preslikava pojaseve Sentinel-3 OLCI B17 (865 nm, "
"bliski infracrveni), B06 (560 nm, zelena) i B03 (442,5 nm, plava) u crveni, "
"zeleni i plavi kanal prikaza. B17 je bliski infracrveni pojas koji se "
"koristi za korekciju aerosola i atmosfere; njegovim postavljanjem u crveni "
"kanal vegetacija i kopnene površine izgledaju jarko crveno, dok voda ostaje "
"tamna. B06 je referentni pojas minimuma apsorpcije klorofila, a B03 bilježi "
"apsorpciju klorofila i biogeokemijska svojstva. U usporedbi s kompozitom "
"B17/B05/B02, pomaknuti zeleni i plavi kanal nude drukčiju osjetljivost na "
"fitoplankton i otopljenu organsku tvar u obalnim i otvorenim oceanskim "
"vodama.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/bands/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to "
"even out the exposure. It makes clouds look natural and keep as much visual "
"information as possible. Sentinel-3 OLCI tiles cover large areas, making it "
"possible to observe large cloud formations, such as hurricanes.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"
msgstr ""
"# Poboljšana vizualizacija prave boje\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta koristi optimizaciju svijetlih dijelova kako bi se izbjegli "
"izgoreni pikseli i izjednačila ekspozicija. Oblaci izgledaju prirodno i "
"zadržava se što više vizualnih informacija. Pločice Sentinel-3 OLCI "
"pokrivaju velika područja, što omogućuje promatranje velikih oblačnih "
"formacija, poput uragana.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/true_color_"
"highlight_optimized/)"

msgid ""
"# Pansharpened True Color\n"
"\n"
"The pansharpened true color composite is done by using the usual true color "
"data (red, green and blue (RGB)) and enhancing them by using the "
"panchromatic band 8, or pan band (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). An image "
"from the pan band is similar to black-and-white film: it combines light "
"from the red, green, and blue parts of the spectrum into a single measure "
"of overall visible reflectance. Pansharpened images have 4x the resolution "
"of the usual true color composite, greatly enhancing the usefulness of "
"Landsat imagery.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."
msgstr ""
"# Pan-izoštrena prava boja\n"
"\n"
"Pan-izoštreni kompozit prave boje izrađuje se korištenjem uobičajenih "
"podataka prave boje (crvena, zelena i plava (RGB)) i njihovim poboljšanjem "
"pomoću pankromatskog pojasa 8, odnosno pan pojasa (pojas je područje "
"elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u "
"različitim pojasevima). Slika iz pan pojasa slična je crno-bijelom filmu: "
"kombinira svjetlost iz crvenog, zelenog i plavog dijela spektra u "
"jedinstvenu mjeru ukupne vidljive refleksije. Pan-izoštrene slike imaju 4 "
"puta veću razlučivost od uobičajenog kompozita prave boje, čime se uvelike "
"povećava korisnost Landsat snimaka.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."

msgid ""
"# False Color Urban composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite is used to visualise urbanized areas more clearly. "
"Vegetation is visible in shades of green, while urbanized areas are "
"represented by white, grey, or purple. Soils, sand, and minerals are shown "
"in a variety of colors. Snow and ice appear as dark blue, and water as "
"black or blue. Flooded areas are very dark blue and almost black. The "
"composite is useful for detecting wildfires and calderas of volcanoes, as "
"they are displayed in shades of red and yellow.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-urban-"
"rgb/) and [here.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit lažnih boja za urbana područja\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj se kompozit koristi za jasniju vizualizaciju urbaniziranih područja. "
"Vegetacija je vidljiva u nijansama zelene, dok su urbanizirana područja "
"prikazana bijelom, sivom ili ljubičastom bojom. Tla, pijesak i minerali "
"prikazani su raznim bojama. Snijeg i led izgledaju tamnoplavo, a voda crno "
"ili plavo. Poplavljena područja su vrlo tamnoplava i gotovo crna. Kompozit "
"je koristan za otkrivanje šumskih požara i kaldera vulkana jer su prikazani "
"u nijansama crvene i žute.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false-color-"
"urban-rgb/) i [ovdje.](https://eos.com/false-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Agriculture composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared, near-infrared and blue bands to "
"monitor crop health (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Both short-wave and "
"near infrared bands are particularly good at highlighting dense vegetation, "
"which appears dark green in the composite. Crops appear in a vibrant green "
"and bare earth appears magenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) and "
"[here.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"
msgstr ""
"# Poljoprivredni kompozit\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit koristi kratkovalni infracrveni, bliski infracrveni i plavi "
"pojas za praćenje zdravlja usjeva (pojas je područje elektromagnetskog "
"spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u različitim pojasevima). I "
"kratkovalni i bliski infracrveni pojas osobito su dobri u isticanju guste "
"vegetacije, koja se u kompozitu prikazuje tamnozelenom bojom. Usjevi se "
"prikazuju živom zelenom bojom, a golo tlo magentom.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija [ovdje](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites) i "
"[ovdje.](https://gisgeography.com/sentinel-2-bands-combinations/)"

msgid ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"The Snow Classifier algorithm aims to detect snow by classifying pixels "
"based on different brightness and Normalized Difference Snow Index (NDSI) "
"thresholds. Values classified as snow are returned in bright vivid blue. "
"The script can overestimate snow areas over clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"
msgstr ""
"# Klasifikator snijega\n"
"\n"
"Algoritam Klasifikator snijega namijenjen je otkrivanju snijega "
"klasifikacijom piksela na temelju različitih pragova svjetline i "
"normaliziranog diferencijalnog indeksa snijega (NDSI). Vrijednosti "
"klasificirane kao snijeg prikazuju se jarkom živom plavom bojom. Skripta "
"može precijeniti područja snijega na oblacima.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/"
")"

msgid ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"The script aims to dynamically visualise the chlorophyll and sediment "
"conditions of water bodies, which are primary indicators of water quality. "
"The chlorophyll content ranges in colors from dark blue (low chlorophyll "
"content) through green to red (high chlorophyll content). Sediment "
"concentrations are colored brown; opaque brown indicates high sediment "
"content.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"
msgstr ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"Skripta je namijenjena dinamičkoj vizualizaciji stanja klorofila i "
"sedimenta u vodenim tijelima, koji su primarni pokazatelji kvalitete vode. "
"Sadržaj klorofila prikazuje se bojama od tamnoplave (nizak sadržaj "
"klorofila) preko zelene do crvene (visok sadržaj klorofila). Koncentracije "
"sedimenta prikazane su smeđom bojom; neprozirna smeđa označava visok "
"sadržaj sedimenta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"

msgid ""
"# Short wave infrared composite (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Short wave infrared (SWIR) measurements can help scientists estimate how "
"much water is present in plants and soil, as water absorbs SWIR "
"wavelengths. Short wave infrared bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) are also useful for distinguishing between cloud types (water clouds "
"versus ice clouds), snow and ice, all of which appear white in visible "
"light. In this composite vegetation appears in shades of green, soils and "
"built-up areas are in various shades of brown, and water appears black. "
"Newly burned land reflects strongly in SWIR bands, making them valuable for "
"mapping fire damages. Each rock type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit kratkovalnog infracrvenog područja (SWIR)\n"
"\n"
"Mjerenja u kratkovalnom infracrvenom području (SWIR) mogu pomoći "
"znanstvenicima da procijene koliko je vode prisutno u biljkama i tlu jer "
"voda apsorbira SWIR valne duljine. Kratkovalni infracrveni pojasevi (pojas "
"je područje elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati "
"Zemlju u različitim pojasevima) korisni su i za razlikovanje vrsta oblaka "
"(vodeni oblaci naspram ledenih oblaka), snijega i leda, koji u vidljivoj "
"svjetlosti svi izgledaju bijelo. U ovom kompozitu vegetacija se prikazuje u "
"nijansama zelene, tla i izgrađena područja u raznim nijansama smeđe, a voda "
"izgleda crno. Tek izgorjelo zemljište snažno reflektira u SWIR pojasevima, "
"zbog čega su oni vrijedni za kartiranje štete od požara. Svaka vrsta "
"stijene drukčije reflektira kratkovalno infracrveno svjetlo, što omogućuje "
"kartiranje geologije usporedbom reflektirane SWIR svjetlosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/swir-rgb/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks snijega (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-2 normalizirani diferencijalni indeks snijega može se koristiti za "
"razlikovanje oblaka i snježnog pokrova jer snijeg apsorbira u kratkovalnom "
"infracrvenom svjetlu, a reflektira vidljivo svjetlo, dok je oblak općenito "
"reflektirajući na obje valne duljine. Snježni pokrov prikazan je jarkom "
"živom plavom bojom.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalised difference snow index (NDSI) can be used to differentiate "
"between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the short-wave infrared "
"light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is generally "
"reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in bright vivid "
"blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks snijega (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani diferencijalni indeks snijega (NDSI) može se koristiti za "
"razlikovanje oblaka i snježnog pokrova jer snijeg apsorbira u kratkovalnom "
"infracrvenom svjetlu, a reflektira vidljivo svjetlo, dok je oblak općenito "
"reflektirajući na obje valne duljine. Snježni pokrov prikazan je jarkom "
"živom plavom bojom.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"This script aims to display the Earth in beautiful natural color images. It "
"uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to even out the "
"exposure.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Prirodne boje optimizirane za svijetle dijelove\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta namijenjena je prikazu Zemlje na lijepim slikama prirodnih "
"boja. Koristi optimizaciju svijetlih dijelova kako bi se izbjegli izgoreni "
"pikseli i izjednačila ekspozicija.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 12, 8, 2 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared (SWIR) band 12 to differentiate "
"among different rock types (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Each rock "
"and mineral type reflects short-wave infrared light differently, making it "
"possible to map out geology by comparing reflected SWIR light. Near "
"infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation and band 2 detects moisture, "
"both contributing to differentiation of ground materials. The composite is "
"useful for finding geological formations and features (e.g. faults, "
"fractures), lithology (e.g. granite, basalt, etc.) and mining applications.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit Geologija 12, 8, 2\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit koristi kratkovalni infracrveni (SWIR) pojas 12 za "
"razlikovanje različitih vrsta stijena (pojas je područje elektromagnetskog "
"spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u različitim pojasevima). "
"Svaka vrsta stijene i minerala drukčije reflektira kratkovalno infracrveno "
"svjetlo, što omogućuje kartiranje geologije usporedbom reflektirane SWIR "
"svjetlosti. Bliski infracrveni (NIR) pojas 8 ističe vegetaciju, a pojas 2 "
"otkriva vlagu, što oboje doprinosi razlikovanju materijala tla. Kompozit je "
"koristan za pronalaženje geoloških formacija i obilježja (npr. rasjeda, "
"pukotina), litologije (npr. granit, bazalt itd.) i rudarskih primjena.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-"
"SWIR.pdf)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 8, 11, 12 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses both short-wave infrared (SWIR) bands 11 and 12 to "
"differentiate among different rock types (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). Each rock and mineral type reflects shortwave infrared light "
"differently, making it possible to map out geology by comparing reflected "
"SWIR light. Near Infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation, contributing "
"to differentiation of ground materials. Vegetation in the composite appears "
"red. The composite is useful for differentiating vegetation, and land "
"especially geologic features that can be useful for mining and mineral "
"exploration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit Geologija 8, 11, 12\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit koristi oba kratkovalna infracrvena (SWIR) pojasa 11 i 12 za "
"razlikovanje različitih vrsta stijena (pojas je područje elektromagnetskog "
"spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u različitim pojasevima). "
"Svaka vrsta stijene i minerala drukčije reflektira kratkovalno infracrveno "
"svjetlo, što omogućuje kartiranje geologije usporedbom reflektirane SWIR "
"svjetlosti. Bliski infracrveni (NIR) pojas 8 ističe vegetaciju, što "
"doprinosi razlikovanju materijala tla. Vegetacija se u kompozitu prikazuje "
"crveno. Kompozit je koristan za razlikovanje vegetacije i zemljišta, "
"osobito geoloških obilježja korisnih za rudarstvo i istraživanje minerala.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](http://murphygeological.com/new---sentinel-2.html#)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, visualizes wildfires using "
"Sentinel-2 data. It combines natural color background with some NIR/SWIR "
"data for smoke penetration and more detail, while adding highlights from "
"B11 and B12 to show fires in red and orange colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"
msgstr ""
"# Šumski požari\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta, koju je izradio Pierre Markuse, vizualizira šumske požare "
"pomoću podataka Sentinel-2. Kombinira pozadinu prirodnih boja s nekim "
"NIR/SWIR podacima za probijanje dima i više detalja, dok dodaje istaknute "
"dijelove iz B11 i B12 kako bi se požari prikazali crvenom i narančastom "
"bojom.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, based on the Pierre Markuse wildfire script, detects and "
"visualizes wildfires using Landsat 8/9 thermal and visible bands. It "
"combines natural color (B2, B3, B4) with thermal band (B10) analysis to "
"detect temperature anomalies and create a red-orange-white glow effect "
"highlighting fire locations.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"
msgstr ""
"# Šumski požari\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta, temeljena na skripti za šumske požare Pierrea Markusea, "
"otkriva i vizualizira šumske požare pomoću termalnih i vidljivih pojaseva "
"Landsat 8/9. Kombinira prirodne boje (B2, B3, B4) s analizom termalnog "
"pojasa (B10) kako bi otkrila temperaturne anomalije i stvorila "
"crveno-narančasto-bijeli efekt sjaja koji ističe lokacije požara.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://github.com/azlinszkysinergise/customscripts_test_az/blob/"
"main/landsat_markuse_fire_v2)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, uses multiple bands (a band is a "
"region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth "
"in different bands) and saturation and brightness control to enhance the "
"true color visualization.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Poboljšana prava boja\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta, koju je izradio Pierre Markuse, koristi više pojaseva (pojas "
"je područje elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati "
"Zemlju u različitim pojasevima) te kontrolu zasićenosti i svjetline za "
"poboljšanje vizualizacije prave boje.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"

msgid ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index takes advantage of the wider spectrum of Visible, "
"Red-Edge, NIR and SWIR bands.\n"
"\n"
"Values description:()=> The range of values for the index is `-1` to `1` "
"for burn scars, and `1` - `6` for active fires. Different fire intensities "
"may result in different thresholds; the current values were calibrated, as "
"per original author, on mostly Mediterranen regions.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"
msgstr ""
"# Indeks opožarenog područja\n"
"\n"
"Indeks opožarenog područja koristi prednosti šireg spektra vidljivih, "
"Red-Edge, NIR i SWIR pojaseva.\n"
"\n"
"Opis vrijednosti:()=> Raspon vrijednosti indeksa je od `-1` do `1` za "
"ožiljke od požara i od `1` do `6` za aktivne požare. Različiti intenziteti "
"požara mogu dati različite pragove; trenutne su vrijednosti, prema izvornom "
"autoru, kalibrirane uglavnom na mediteranskim regijama.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Burn Ratio is frequently used to estimate burn severity. It uses "
"near-infrared (NIR) and shortwave-infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. Healthy "
"vegetation has a high reflectance in the near-infrared portion of the "
"spectrum, and a low short-wave infrared reflectance. On the other hand, "
"burned areas have a high shortwave infrared reflectance but low reflectance "
"in the near infrared Darker pixels indicate burned areas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizirani omjer opožarenosti (NBR)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizirani omjer opožarenosti često se koristi za procjenu težine "
"opožarenosti. Koristi bliske infracrvene (NIR) i kratkovalne infracrvene "
"(SWIR) valne duljine. Zdrava vegetacija ima visoku refleksiju u bliskom "
"infracrvenom dijelu spektra i nisku refleksiju u kratkovalnom infracrvenom. "
"S druge strane, opožarena područja imaju visoku refleksiju u kratkovalnom "
"infracrvenom, ali nisku u bliskom infracrvenom. Tamniji pikseli označavaju "
"opožarena područja.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"nbr/)."

msgid ""
"# Atmospheric penetration\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses different bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) in the non-visible part of the electromagnetic spectrum to reduce "
"the influence of the atmosphere in the image. Short wave infrared bands 11 "
"and 12 are highly reflected by the heated areas, making them useful for "
"fire and burned area mapping. Near infrared band 8, is on contrary, highly "
"reflected by vegetation, which signifies absence of fire. Vegetation "
"appears blue, displaying details related to the vegetation vigor. Healthy "
"vegetation is shown in light blue while the stressed, sparse or/and arid "
"vegetation appears in dull blue. Urban features are white, grey, cyan or "
"purple.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosferska penetracija\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit koristi različite pojaseve (pojas je područje "
"elektromagnetskog spektra; satelitski senzor može snimati Zemlju u "
"različitim pojasevima) u nevidljivom dijelu elektromagnetskog spektra kako "
"bi smanjio utjecaj atmosfere na sliku. Kratkovalni infracrveni pojasevi 11 "
"i 12 snažno se reflektiraju od zagrijanih područja, zbog čega su korisni za "
"kartiranje požara i opožarenih područja. Bliski infracrveni pojas 8, "
"naprotiv, snažno reflektira vegetacija, što znači odsutnost požara. "
"Vegetacija se prikazuje plavo i otkriva detalje povezane sa snagom "
"vegetacije. Zdrava vegetacija prikazana je svijetloplavo, dok rijetka, "
"stresom pogođena i/ili sušna vegetacija izgleda mutnoplavo. Urbana "
"obilježja su bijela, siva, cijan ili ljubičasta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija [ovdje.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"

msgid ""
"# Barren Soil Visualization\n"
"\n"
"The Barren Soil Visualization can be useful for soil mapping, to "
"investigate the location of landslides or the extent of erosion in "
"non-vegetated areas. This visualization shows all vegetation in green and "
"the barren ground in red. Water appears black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) and "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizacija neplodnog tla\n"
"\n"
"Vizualizacija neplodnog tla može biti korisna za kartiranje tla, "
"istraživanje lokacije klizišta ili opsega erozije na područjima bez "
"vegetacije. Ova vizualizacija prikazuje svu vegetaciju zeleno, a neplodno "
"tlo crveno. Voda izgleda crno.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) i "
"[ovdje.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"

msgid ""
"# True Color with IR Highlights composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite enhances the true color visualization by adding the "
"shortwave infrared wavelengths to amplify details. It displays heated areas "
"in red/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"
msgstr ""
"# Kompozit prave boje s IR isticanjem\n"
"\n"
"Ovaj kompozit poboljšava vizualizaciju prave boje dodavanjem kratkovalnih "
"infracrvenih valnih duljina radi isticanja detalja. Zagrijana područja "
"prikazuje crveno/narančasto.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-"
"space-9d1de0133733)"

msgid ""
"# Detection of Burned Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script is used to detect large scale recently burned areas. Pixels "
"colored red highlight burned areas, and all other pixels are returned in "
"true color. The script sometimes overestimates burned areas over water and "
"clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"
msgstr ""
"# Otkrivanje opožarenih područja\n"
"\n"
"Ova se skripta koristi za otkrivanje nedavno opožarenih područja velikih "
"razmjera. Pikseli obojeni crveno ističu opožarena područja, a svi ostali "
"pikseli prikazuju se u pravoj boji. Skripta ponekad precjenjuje opožarena "
"područja iznad vode i oblaka.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"

msgid ""
"# Scene classification\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Scene classification was developed to distinguish between cloudy pixels, "
"clear pixels and water pixels of Sentinel-2 data and is a result of ESA's "
"Scene classification algorithm. Twelve different classifications are "
"provided including classes of clouds, vegetation, soils/desert, water and "
"snow. It does not constitute a land cover classification map in a strict "
"sense.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."
msgstr ""
"# Klasifikacija scene\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Klasifikacija scene razvijena je za razlikovanje oblačnih piksela, čistih "
"piksela i piksela vode u podacima Sentinel-2 te je rezultat ESA-inog "
"algoritma za klasifikaciju scene. Pruža se dvanaest različitih "
"klasifikacija, uključujući klase oblaka, vegetacije, tla/pustinje, vode i "
"snijega. Ne predstavlja kartu pokrova zemljišta u strogom smislu.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/scene-"
"classification/)."

msgid ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI) is estimated based on the "
"chlorophyll content in terrestrial vegetation and can be used to monitor "
"vegetation condition and health. Low OTCI values usually signify water, "
"sand or snow. Extremely high values, displayed with white, usually suggest "
"the absence of chlorophyll as well. They generally represent either bare "
"ground, rock or clouds. The chlorophyll values in between range from red "
"(low chlorophyll values) to dark green (high chlorophyll values) can be "
"used to determine vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"
msgstr ""
"# Indeks kopnenog klorofila (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Indeks kopnenog klorofila (OTCI) procjenjuje se na temelju sadržaja "
"klorofila u kopnenoj vegetaciji i može se koristiti za praćenje stanja i "
"zdravlja vegetacije. Niske vrijednosti OTCI-ja obično označavaju vodu, "
"pijesak ili snijeg. Izrazito visoke vrijednosti, prikazane bijelom bojom, "
"obično upućuju i na odsutnost klorofila. Općenito predstavljaju golo tlo, "
"stijene ili oblake. Vrijednosti klorofila između, od crvene (niske "
"vrijednosti klorofila) do tamnozelene (visoke vrijednosti klorofila), mogu "
"se koristiti za određivanje zdravlja vegetacije.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"

msgid ""
"# Topographic Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a visualisation with green colours representing lowland "
"elevations and earth colours as mountainous elevations. The script uses "
"discrete classes rather than the continuous visualisations in the other DEM "
"layers.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"
msgstr ""
"# Topografska vizualizacija\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta vraća vizualizaciju u kojoj zelene boje predstavljaju nizinske "
"visine, a zemljane boje planinske visine. Skripta koristi diskretne klase "
"umjesto kontinuiranih vizualizacija u ostalim DEM slojevima.\n"
"\n"
"U evalscriptu je moguće postaviti prilagođene minimalne i maksimalne "
"vrijednosti postavljanjem defaultVis na false i postavljanjem varijabli min "
"i max na željene vrijednosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-topographic/)"

msgid ""
"# Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a color visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizacija u boji\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta vraća vizualizaciju digitalnog modela reljefa u boji, "
"dodjeljujući kontinuirane boje granicama visina.\n"
"\n"
"U evalscriptu je moguće postaviti prilagođene minimalne i maksimalne "
"vrijednosti postavljanjem defaultVis na false i postavljanjem varijabli min "
"i max na željene vrijednosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-color/)"

msgid ""
"# Grayscale Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a grayscale visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"
msgstr ""
"# Vizualizacija u sivim tonovima\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta vraća vizualizaciju digitalnog modela reljefa u sivim tonovima, "
"dodjeljujući kontinuirane boje granicama visina.\n"
"\n"
"U evalscriptu je moguće postaviti prilagođene minimalne i maksimalne "
"vrijednosti postavljanjem defaultVis na false i postavljanjem varijabli min "
"i max na željene vrijednosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-grayscale/)"

msgid ""
"# Sepia Visualization\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"This script returns a sepia visualization of a digital elevation model, "
"assigning continuous colors to the elevation borders.\n"
"\n"
"It is possible to set custom min and max values in the evalscript by "
"setting defaultVis to false and setting the min and max variables to the "
"desired values.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"
msgstr ""
"# Sepija vizualizacija\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta vraća sepija vizualizaciju digitalnog modela reljefa, "
"dodjeljujući kontinuirane boje granicama visina.\n"
"\n"
"U evalscriptu je moguće postaviti prilagođene minimalne i maksimalne "
"vrijednosti postavljanjem defaultVis na false i postavljanjem varijabli min "
"i max na željene vrijednosti.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/dem/dem-sepia/)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It displays water areas in blue (partially black) and "
"land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban areas are displayed in a "
"light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas in mustard green and "
"bare ground in a darker green.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. In order not to confuse "
"cryogenic features with non-cryogenic ones, some general information about "
"the location is helpful in interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# Poboljšana vizualizacija\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta kombinira gamma0 VV i VH polarizacija u vizualizaciju lažnih "
"boja. Vodena područja prikazuje plavo (djelomično crno), a kopno u "
"različitim nijansama žute/zelene. Urbana područja prikazana su "
"svijetlozeleno-žutom bojom (prema bijeloj), područja s vegetacijom "
"gorušičino zelenom, a golo tlo tamnijom zelenom.\n"
"\n"
"Za snježna i ledena područja vizualizacija može varirati od "
"svijetlozeleno-žute preko svjetlije zelene do tamnosmeđe ili čak crne. Kako "
"se kriogene pojave ne bi zamijenile s nekriogenima, za tumačenje slike "
"korisne su neke opće informacije o lokaciji."

msgid ""
"# SAR False Color Visualization\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations of "
"Sentinel-1 SAR data into a false color visualization. Water areas appear in "
"blue (partially black) and land in different shades of yellow/green. Urban "
"areas are displayed in light green-yellow (towards white), vegetated areas "
"in mustard green, and bare ground in darker green. The visualization "
"supports a wide range of monitoring applications, including ice and ship "
"tracking, agriculture and deforestation monitoring, and emergency response "
"scenarios such as flood and volcano observation.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light green-yellow "
"over brighter green to dark brown or even black. Some general knowledge of "
"the location is helpful to avoid confusing cryogenic features with other "
"land cover types.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR vizualizacija lažnih boja\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta kombinira gamma0 VV i VH polarizacija Sentinel-1 SAR podataka u "
"vizualizaciju lažnih boja. Vodena područja izgledaju plavo (djelomično "
"crno), a kopno u različitim nijansama žute/zelene. Urbana područja "
"prikazana su svijetlozeleno-žutom bojom (prema bijeloj), područja s "
"vegetacijom gorušičino zelenom, a golo tlo tamnijom zelenom. Vizualizacija "
"podržava širok raspon primjena praćenja, uključujući praćenje leda i "
"brodova, praćenje poljoprivrede i krčenja šuma te scenarije hitnog "
"djelovanja poput promatranja poplava i vulkana.\n"
"\n"
"Za snježna i ledena područja vizualizacija može varirati od "
"svijetlozeleno-žute preko svjetlije zelene do tamnosmeđe ili čak crne. "
"Određeno opće poznavanje lokacije korisno je kako se kriogene pojave ne bi "
"zamijenile s drugim vrstama pokrova zemljišta.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_false_color_"
"visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# Urban Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script uses Sentinel-1 SAR VH and VV polarisations to highlight urban "
"areas and buildings. Structures appear in different colours depending on "
"their backscatter characteristics: purple indicates high VH reflectance, "
"green indicates high VV reflectance, and white indicates high reflectance "
"in both. The red channel is restricted to pixels where VH exceeds 0.5, "
"helping separate buildings from bare soil. The script is useful for "
"monitoring urban expansion, assessing building density, and identifying "
"structures in flood-prone areas. Note that in mountainous terrain, steep "
"slopes and snow can produce similar signals, making it difficult to "
"separate urban areas from other features.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# Urbana područja\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta koristi Sentinel-1 SAR VH i VV polarizacije za isticanje "
"urbanih područja i zgrada. Strukture se pojavljuju u različitim bojama "
"ovisno o svojim značajkama povratnog raspršenja: ljubičasta označava visoku "
"VH refleksiju, zelena visoku VV refleksiju, a bijela visoku refleksiju u "
"obje. Crveni kanal ograničen je na piksele u kojima VH premašuje 0,5, što "
"pomaže razdvojiti zgrade od golog tla. Skripta je korisna za praćenje "
"širenja urbanih područja, procjenu gustoće izgrađenosti i prepoznavanje "
"struktura u područjima sklonima poplavama. Imajte na umu da u planinskom "
"terenu strme padine i snijeg mogu davati slične signale, što otežava "
"razdvajanje urbanih područja od drugih obilježja.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# SAR Deforestation Detection\n"
"\n"
"This script processes Sentinel-1 VV and VH polarisation bands to detect "
"deforestation and forest degradation. It converts the backscatter values "
"into polar form to derive vector length and angle, which discriminate "
"between water, forest, and bare soil. Water and bare soil appear black, "
"forested areas are rendered in green gradients, and degraded or cleared "
"areas appear in red — with stronger colours indicating higher "
"classification confidence. The script is useful for monitoring forest loss "
"and land-use change over time.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_deforestation_"
"detection/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR otkrivanje krčenja šuma\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta obrađuje Sentinel-1 VV i VH polarizacijske pojaseve radi "
"otkrivanja krčenja šuma i degradacije šuma. Pretvara vrijednosti povratnog "
"raspršenja u polarni oblik kako bi dobila duljinu vektora i kut, koji "
"razlikuju vodu, šumu i golo tlo. Voda i golo tlo izgledaju crno, šumska "
"područja prikazana su zelenim gradijentima, a degradirana ili očišćena "
"područja crveno — pri čemu jače boje označavaju veću pouzdanost "
"klasifikacije. Skripta je korisna za praćenje gubitka šuma i promjena "
"namjene zemljišta tijekom vremena.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/sar_"
"deforestation_detection/)."

msgid ""
"# Water Surface Roughness\n"
"\n"
"This script visualizes water surface roughness using Sentinel-1 SAR data. "
"SAR backscatter is highly sensitive to the roughness of the water surface: "
"calm water reflects radar energy away from the sensor and appears dark, "
"while rough or wind-driven water scatters energy back and appears brighter. "
"Variations in surface roughness reveal oceanographic and maritime features "
"such as wind patterns, sea currents, internal waves, and ship wakes. Oil "
"spills dampen surface waves and appear as dark patches against the "
"surrounding rougher water. The visualization supports maritime monitoring "
"applications including ship tracking, oil pollution detection, and "
"observation of ocean circulation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."
msgstr ""
"# Hrapavost vodene površine\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta vizualizira hrapavost vodene površine pomoću Sentinel-1 SAR "
"podataka. SAR povratno raspršenje vrlo je osjetljivo na hrapavost vodene "
"površine: mirna voda reflektira radarsku energiju od senzora i izgleda "
"tamno, dok hrapava voda ili voda koju pokreće vjetar raspršuje energiju "
"natrag i izgleda svjetlije. Varijacije hrapavosti površine otkrivaju "
"oceanografska i pomorska obilježja poput uzoraka vjetra, morskih struja, "
"unutarnjih valova i tragova brodova. Izlijevanja nafte priguše površinske "
"valove i izgledaju kao tamne mrlje na okolnoj hrapavijoj vodi. "
"Vizualizacija podržava primjene pomorskog nadzora, uključujući praćenje "
"brodova, otkrivanje onečišćenja naftom i promatranje oceanske cirkulacije.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/water_surface_"
"roughness_visualization/)."

msgid ""
"# RGB ratio\n"
"\n"
"This script combines the gamma0 of the VV and VH polarizations into a false "
"color visualization. It uses the VV polarization in the red channel, the VH "
"polarization in the green channel, and a ratio of VH/VV in the blue "
"channel. It shows water areas in dark red (black), urban areas in yellow, "
"vegetated areas in turquoise, and bare ground in dark purple.\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from light yellow to "
"blue to red. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with non-cryogenic "
"ones, some general information about the location is helpful in "
"interpreting the image."
msgstr ""
"# RGB omjer\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta kombinira gamma0 VV i VH polarizacija u vizualizaciju lažnih "
"boja. Koristi VV polarizaciju u crvenom kanalu, VH polarizaciju u zelenom "
"kanalu i omjer VH/VV u plavom kanalu. Vodena područja prikazuje tamnocrveno "
"(crno), urbana područja žuto, područja s vegetacijom tirkizno, a golo tlo "
"tamnoljubičasto.\n"
"\n"
"Za snježna i ledena područja vizualizacija može varirati od svijetložute "
"preko plave do crvene. Kako se kriogene pojave ne bi zamijenile s "
"nekriogenima, za tumačenje slike korisne su neke opće informacije o "
"lokaciji."

msgid ""
"# SAR Urban\n"
"\n"
"The script is useful for locating urban areas and individual buildings. It "
"uses the gamma0 of the VH polarization and the VV polarizations to "
"highlight different buildings and topology orientations with purple and "
"green colors. It can be used to track urban expansion, estimate building "
"type, or locate buildings in risk areas (e.g., flooding).\n"
"\n"
"For snowy and icy areas, the visualization can vary from white to purple to "
"dark blue or even black. In order not to confuse cryogenic features with "
"non-cryogenic ones, some general information about the location is helpful "
"to interpret the image. \n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."
msgstr ""
"# SAR urbano\n"
"\n"
"Skripta je korisna za lociranje urbanih područja i pojedinačnih zgrada. "
"Koristi gamma0 VH polarizacije i VV polarizacije kako bi ljubičastom i "
"zelenom bojom istaknula različite zgrade i orijentacije topologije. Može se "
"koristiti za praćenje širenja urbanih područja, procjenu vrste zgrada ili "
"lociranje zgrada u rizičnim područjima (npr. od poplava).\n"
"\n"
"Za snježna i ledena područja vizualizacija može varirati od bijele preko "
"ljubičaste do tamnoplave ili čak crne. Kako se kriogene pojave ne bi "
"zamijenile s nekriogenima, za tumačenje slike korisne su neke opće "
"informacije o lokaciji. \n"
"\n"
"Više informacija "
"[ovdje](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-1/urban_areas/)."

msgid ""
"# HH - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships. It provides good contrast between water and "
"land surfaces. Compared to the linear gamma0 visualization, the decibel "
"gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HH - decibelski gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta prikazuje vizualizaciju gamma0 HH polarizacije u sivim "
"tonovima. HH polarizacija manje je osjetljiva na hrapavost površine u "
"usporedbi s VV polarizacijom pa se stoga koristi za otkrivanje objekata i "
"tvrdih ciljeva poput brodova. Pruža dobar kontrast između vodenih i "
"kopnenih površina. U usporedbi s linearnom vizualizacijom gamma0, "
"decibelska vizualizacija gamma0 uključuje logaritamsko skaliranje podataka."

msgid ""
"# HH - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HH "
"polarization. The HH polarization is less sensitive to surface roughness "
"compared to the VV polarization and is therefore used for detecting objects "
"and hard targets such as ships."
msgstr ""
"# HH - linearni gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta prikazuje vizualizaciju gamma0 HH polarizacije u sivim "
"tonovima. HH polarizacija manje je osjetljiva na hrapavost površine u "
"usporedbi s VV polarizacijom pa se stoga koristi za otkrivanje objekata i "
"tvrdih ciljeva poput brodova."

msgid ""
"# HV - decibel gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
"the visualization) and lower for surfaces with little to no scattering "
"(darker color in the visualization). Compared to the linear gamma0 "
"visualization, the decibel gamma0 visualization includes a logarithmic "
"scaling of the data."
msgstr ""
"# HV - decibelski gamma0\n"
"\n"
"Ova skripta prikazuje vizualizaciju gamma0 HV polarizacije u sivim "
"tonovima. Vrijednosti za unakrsnu polarizaciju (HV) općenito su niže "
"(tamnija vizualizacija) nego za supolarizaciju (HH, VV). HV polarizacija "
"ima više vrijednosti za površine obilježene volumnim raspršenjem, npr. "
"grane, suha tijela tla ili krošnje (svjetlija boja u vizualizaciji), a niže "
"za površine s malo ili nimalo raspršenja (tamnija boja u vizualizaciji). U "
"usporedbi s linearnom vizualizacijom gamma0, decibelska vizualizacija "
"gamma0 uključuje logaritamsko skaliranje podataka."

msgid ""
"# HV - linear gamma0\n"
"\n"
"This script displays a grayscale visualization of the gamma0 of the HV "
"polarization. The values for the cross polarization (HV) are generally "
"lower (darker visualization) than for the co-polarization (HH, VV). The HV "
"polarization has higher values for surfaces characterized by volume "
"scattering, e.g., branches, dry coil bodies, or canopies (lighter color in "
